{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms","id":990170,"title":"Question about supernal realms vs other realms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-19T17:31:01-07:00","id":990170,"title":"Question about supernal realms vs other realms","content":"Apologies since this has been discussed before, but I'm trying to get a handle on this, since I've been rereading Changeling. So, 2e has done a lot to sort of cut through the confusion on the realms, and specifying that the Arcadias aren't the same. So, is the general, basic assumption that the supernal realms aren't actual places, they're sort of...clusters of symbols that manifest within the soul/mind of the Mage when they Awaken? <br /> <br /> To give another example, the Empyrean isn't so much connected to the God-Machine or the Principle as it is an abstract conception of the same symbols, images, and concepts that comprise them? And Mage Arcadia isn't the same as Changeling Arcadia, because it isn't actually a place, but they're similar in that they both relate to similar concepts? So the Wyrd and Arcadia are physical manifestations of the concepts of fate and narrative, while Mage Arcadia is also related to those concepts, but in the sense that their presence in the world causes them to form into a &quot;realm&quot; in the Supernal?<br /> <br /> Awakening is kind of super confusing and weird when you get into it, but I'm not saying that as a criticism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-21-2016, 01:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T17:42:11-07:00","id":990175,"title":"","content":"The Supernal Realms aren't really places but clusters of symbols and associated truths that happen to fit together nicely enough to provide a road to Awakening in a human mind/soul, though they may or may not have existed in a more tangible way in the nonexistent time before the Fall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T17:53:37-07:00","id":990177,"title":"","content":"They also could be actual places since they are clusters of symbols that manifest within the soul/mind and there is a place that can be visited that is made wholly of that: The Astral Realms. Theoretically, the Supernal would be at the farthest part of the Astral, beyond the Abyss. But no regular Mages have ever made it there (the Awakening possibly being an exception).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T18:12:36-07:00","id":990185,"title":"","content":"Theoretically, even the specific symbolic groupings common of the various realms are only arbitrarily linked thanks to the Watchtowers. IIRC from Imperial Mysteries, the Watchtowers act as Lustrums during the initial awakening, filtering the symbols an individual mage is allowed to perceive into only (or at least mostly) the symbols relevant to what's typically known as a mages Path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T18:37:48-07:00","id":990194,"title":"","content":"I could talk about how the phenomenon of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hierophany\" target=\"_blank\">hierophany</a> is broadly salient here, but the short and long of it is that the Supernal is a transcendent realm that manifests through symbols that happen to be used by other realms for similar reasons.<br /> <br /> Just as Beasts derive Kinship Nightmares from the core of &quot;what elements of fear are associated with this being I am tied to?&quot; regardless of whether the Primordial Dream is the actual root of the supernatural, the Supernal is the collection of grains of occult power that the Awakened glimpse at the heart of magical phenomena.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T18:38:33-07:00","id":990196,"title":"","content":"As I understand it, there is a difference between the Supernal <i>world</i> and the Supernal <i>realms</i>. The Supernal world is what Mages see when they use Mage Sight, the symbolic truths that define and are given meaning by the Fallen world. The Supernal realms are the hypothetical places from whence these symbols originate, which may or may not actually exist, and if they do, probably aren't &quot;places&quot; in the traditional sense of the word where it's a physical space you can occupy, but are more like cosmic addresses that exist beyond the Fallen world.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To explain it in terms of the allegory of the cave, the Fallen world is the wall and the shadows being cast on it. The Supernal world is the cut outs being used to cast the shadows. The Supernal Realms are outside the cave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-19-2016, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T19:20:25-07:00","id":990210,"title":"","content":"Eh, I kind of prefer them not really being a physical place, and definitely not something that takes precedence over everything else. The &quot;symbols manifested within the mind of the Mage&quot; approach is one I really like, and I'm glad 2e has a lot of support for it, because it doesn't privilege the Mage cosmology over any other one. For example, if Fae Arcadia and Mage Arcadia are both places, then you have &quot;the real shiny true Arcadia and the shitty fake pathetic reflection of Arcadia for losers&quot;, whereas &quot;Mage Arcadia is a symbolic representation of the ideals of time and fate that a Mage creates within themself to connect their soul to the Supernal, which resembles Mage Arcadia to a point because it both draw from similar pools of symbols&quot;. I can see the cave allegory being something some mages tell themselves, but out of universe I don't really think it works out, unless the Supernal is the only kind of magic in the your setting. <br /> <br /> I guess I'm just a crossover person, but I have heard a lot about how Awakening is crossover-compatible, and how quite a few Mysteries aren't connected to the Supernal and relate to other supernatural phenomena. I've also heard that mages don't approach them from the perspective of &quot;oh look at these silly little fake versions of the Supernal realms&quot;, and going deep into the symbols approach seems like a good way to do it, allowing mages to study and comprehend other supernatural phenomena and connect it to their own understanding of the world, without making either cosmology subservient to the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T19:48:43-07:00","id":990217,"title":"","content":"I'm not very much into crossover aside from using other game lines as antagonists, so the idea of the Supernal Realms being a real and physical place is perfectly fine with me. The war that the Seers of the Throne won over the Diamond Orders (the Nameless Orders not being a thing back then) plays nicely into this. The Exarchs rule over the Supernal Realms while the Oracles fight their pitiful guerrilla warfare in the shadows. Entire pocket realms have been built between the Fallen World, incapable of withstanding the existence of Ministers, and the Supernal Realms. From on high the Ministers speak to their loyal subjects, and they in turn speak with the god-like Exarchs who aren't satisfied with simple pocket realms. They rule over the entire known cosmos.<br /> <br /> No ordinary mage is capable of traversing across the Abyss to the Supernal Realms, but being able to summon servants from these Realms through the Watchtowers is proof positive that they exist.<br /> <br /> Or, maybe, it's all just Seer propaganda. Anyhow, like I said, I'm a big fan of the Seers of the Throne. Even though their faction book is really boring to read it has a lot of ideas that I like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","user":"TelperionST","date":".  Typo 10-19-2016, 10:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T20:03:20-07:00","id":990223,"title":"","content":"Okay, that's fine if it's your preference, but the second edition does seem to be pushing back against the idea that the Supernal realms are physical places- similarly, second edition devs have been very open about wanting to make the backstory and mythology, especially Atlantis, much more open and ambiguous. <br /> <br /> Being able to summon Supernal beings doesn't necessary equal the realms being actual physical places, too. It could easily be that the Mage is grabbing a handful of ideas and symbols and physically manifesting them in the world. <br /> <br /> I guess it comes down to preference, ultimately, regarding the game and crossovers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T20:17:43-07:00","id":990227,"title":"","content":"Supernal Realms being places or not is ultimately academic, because it won't matter in almost any game that you're actually in. It's sort of like the true cosmological nature of Duat from Mummy, or debating where the denizens of the underworld who never lived come from - good for a debate, but ultimately besides the point, so I wouldn't get too wrapped up in that.<br /> <br /> The most relateable analogy I've heard so far is from DaveB a long while back about how Awakening relates to the Matrix: mages are redpills, in that they are aware that their reality is a simulation and have the power to bend or break the artificial rules. The big difference? The Supernal isn't the real world, the Supernal is the source code that Neo can see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T20:22:31-07:00","id":990228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990223#post990223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, that's fine if it's your preference, but the second edition does seem to be pushing back against the idea that the Supernal realms are physical places</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, &quot;the Supernal Realms are 'realms'&quot; is not mutually exclusive with &quot;the Supernal Realms are not physical locations&quot; \u2014 <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reality_in_Buddhism#Reality_and_dreams_in_Dzogchen\" target=\"_blank\">Space is one of the Gross Arcana</a>, after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imperial Mysteries, p28: &quot;The Supernal Realms&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Supernal Realms are not places as mortals think of them, but a near-infinite collection of platonic truths, each informing an aspect of Fallen reality. Anything \u2014 including mages and archmages \u2014 exposed to the raw power of the Supernal is either obliterated or absorbed, with the ententes debating the difference among themselves since time immemorial. As the origin for the Arcana, the Realms lack the frames of reference needed for a living mind to make sense of them \u2014 there are no set rules of Time and Space, for example, as both Arcana are produced in the Supernal, so even the process of \u201cgoing somewhere\u201d is impossible without some form of filtering.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T20:27:52-07:00","id":990230,"title":"","content":"Eh, I've never really liked the Matrix analogy because A. Neo isn't a monster and B. It reinforces the &quot;mages see the whole deeper truth that none of the other supernaturals can see&quot; thing. But that's getting into another issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T20:32:46-07:00","id":990231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990223#post990223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, that's fine if it's your preference, but the second edition does seem to be pushing back against the idea that the Supernal realms are physical places- similarly, second edition devs have been very open about wanting to make the backstory and mythology, especially Atlantis, much more open and ambiguous.</div> </div> </div> </div>O' I definitely noticed that shift in the core book. There is a lot more ambiguity built right into the book, and I like the fact that it's there. However, a decade ago I was still playing a lot of Mage: the Ascension, which had these majestic, interdimentional, reality breaking wars. Mage 1E has a lot of that built right into the mythos and I like it that way. I may be in the minority, but I like the Atlantis mythology. Mage is the game that screams: go big, or go home! I really like this game, because I can use the craziest, most imaginitive, storylines and they fit perfectly into the game. Right down to interdimentional cthulhu-esq mad gods trying to break into our reality, city-sized ancient dragons slumbering unnoticed throughout the ages, immortal beings traveling across the Fallen World in endless circles of chaos and disruption, genies in a bottle, flying carpets and guns with no real bullets that still kill people. 2E has a more down to earth feel to it, but at the same time it doesn't try and stop me from having fun with this game. That's why I got fed up with Mage: the Ascension. However, that's an entirely different topic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T20:34:51-07:00","id":990233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990230#post990230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I've never really liked the Matrix analogy because A. Neo isn't a monster and B. It reinforces the &quot;mages see the whole deeper truth that none of the other supernaturals can see&quot; thing. But that's getting into another issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Analogies don't map 1:1. And in this particular case, Mages -can- see a whole deeper truth that no one else can see. It's...the Supernal. They're the only ones that interact with it.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean there isn't other weird supernatural stuff going on out there, including entire realms classified by Mages by how little they understand them, but in this particular case I feel like the analogy illustrates the flavor of gnosticism at work in the game, how it relates to mages and what the role of the Supernal is in their narrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T20:35:31-07:00","id":990234,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I guess I generally prefer that ChroD games in general maintain that street-level focus and &quot;nobody is really in control&quot; feeling.<br /> <br /> And if Mages are really the only ones who can perceive and interact with the Supernal, I don't really like that, and I like making it primarily a symbolic thing to keep it from being &quot;the special mage-only world that only mages can see and is the most important thing&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T20:44:44-07:00","id":990238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990234#post990234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if Mages are really the only ones who can perceive and interact with the Supernal, I don't really like that, and I like making it primarily a symbolic thing to keep it from being &quot;the special mage-only world that only mages can see and is the most important thing&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue that you have, that many people who dislike this game as well as those that overemphasize Mage's role in the CofD also make, is that because the Supernal is the underlying blocks of reality and only mages can mess with it, that it's the most important thing.<br /> <br /> Another analogy: just because physicists and chemists have a lifetime of study and specialized tools to observe things on an atomic level doesn't make physicists the most important people in the world, even though atoms are the building blocks of everything, even if they DID know everything. And they don't. They super, super don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T20:49:11-07:00","id":990240,"title":"","content":"Has anyone mentioned yet that the upcoming supplement will be addressing the Supernal as place thing, with 2e's version of Emanations? These are actual Supernal places that mages can visit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-19-2016, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T20:51:19-07:00","id":990241,"title":"","content":"The problem is, anyone can be a physicist or understand atoms. The game generally tends to be pretty bad about emphasizing that only mages can understand or interact with the Supernal, and even though there are other magical domains they can still ultimately understand them. <br /> <br /> And the problem if you rule &quot;they're completely separate&quot; is that it's somewhat inelegant. If there's no connection between the Arcadias, then that's a bit awkward. If you talk up how mages know all of this about the building blocks of reality and so on, and then say that &quot;no, the other Magic is completely different&quot;, that's kind of an inelegant solution. <br /> <br /> The reason I like the &quot;symbols&quot; view is that it allows the Supernal to be connected to other forms of magic without subsuming them. <br /> <br /> And yes, you can make the argument that the most fundamental building block of something is the most important part of it.<br /> <br /> And about Emanations, you can describe that the same way you can rationalize summoning: 2e emphasizes that magic manipulates truths, so you can see bringing &quot;Supernal&quot; beings or phenomena into the world as using magic to add truth to symbols. <br /> <br /> To use another specific example, a Supernal entity that resembles a Fae isn't an actual Fae, but it isn't actually a being from Other Better Arcadia: it's the Mage using the ability of their magic to create &quot;truth&quot; to give substance to the ideas of narrative, capriciousness, and fate, which connects those with related thematic symbols and forms them into a shape that resembles other supernatural beings also informed by those ideals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-20-2016, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T21:04:12-07:00","id":990242,"title":"","content":"To be clear, I'm not arguing for or against any particular interpretation of the Supernal, only that even IF it was a real, actual place, the only people who can actually visit it are the handful of arcane demigods who achieved archmastery and the literal plot devices that live on the other side of the Supernal veil. It's a moot point, practically speaking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990241#post990241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, you can make the argument that the most fundamental building block of something is the most important part of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet we don't have physicist-kings, and being able to observe stuff on the atomic level isn't going to automatically solve any of the obstacles in your daily life.<br /> <br /> Like, I'm not going to say that mage sight is useless or anything, but I am trying to provide some amount of perspective on what that special knowledge actually provides and what it means in the grand scheme of things, ESPECIALLY from the perspective of crossover. The most pernicious misunderstanding that the game has faced, both for detractors and overenthusiastic fans, is overemphasizing just how important knowing the Secret Nature Of The Universe(tm) actually is. Mages often are written in that way as well, but it's worth noting that mages, by and large, are smug know-it-alls who like to put things in neat little boxes even when they shouldn't be - again, the Lower Depths are a category of &quot;realms&quot; that are defined partially by how little the Supernal actually matters to them and partially by how little mages understand them. It's a game of hubris and reach exceeding grasp, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T21:07:07-07:00","id":990243,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't want to get into an argument and I understand that it's all a matter of what the individual wants. There Is No Canon and all that. But I do think that &quot;it doesn't matter because it's just a background element that won't come into play in your game&quot; doesn't work out at all when you're talking about a game that involves investigating cosmic mysteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T21:16:02-07:00","id":990244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990241#post990241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you talk up how mages know all of this about the building blocks of reality and so on, and then say that &quot;no, the other Magic is completely different&quot;, that's kind of an inelegant solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>The letter &quot;a&quot; appears nine times in this sentence, including all the instances where I just say &quot;a&quot; to be clear that I'm referring to the letter &quot;a.&quot;<br /> <br /> The thing about the building blocks of reality is that they're really fucking small and one's ability to convey them is constrained by language. Language is messy and magic is messier still.<br /> <br /> Mages understand other realms through what their Supernal understanding allows them to glean, which, while fairly comprehensive, is never going to give them the kind of instinctive grasp of those metaphysics that its natives or part-natives possess by virtue of direct integration with those frameworks. No Traveler's Mastery of Fate will allow them to learn Contracts and no ordinary Tremere is going to start manifesting Disciplines.<br /> <br /> And for the most part mages <i>don't</i> interact with the Supernal \u2014 looking at the symbolic forms of transcendent reality and drawing them forth with spellcraft doesn't translate to the kind of broad-reaching influence that, say, werewolves have through interaction with the Shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T21:20:41-07:00","id":990246,"title":"","content":"Okay then. That's...pretty much what I was saying I would like? I think one of my major problems is in terminology: referring to everything that isn't Supernal as &quot;fallen&quot; or &quot;the lie&quot; and everyone who isn't a Mage as &quot;unawakened&quot; probably contributes more to people seeing Mage supremacy than anything in the actual content, honestly. It would be nice if the books could be a bit more overt that those terms are mostly used by mages out of egotism. Dave went on a tear in one thread about how much he hates people assuming that mages look at all other supernatural phenomena as subordinate to the Supernal and beneath it, but it's kind of inevitable that people are going to assume that when that's the language that mages and the books use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T21:25:53-07:00","id":990250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990210#post990210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I kind of prefer them not really being a physical place, and definitely not something that takes precedence over everything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are most definitely not physical places, and they don't take precedence over everything else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990210#post990210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;symbols manifested within the mind of the Mage&quot; approach is one I really like, and I'm glad 2e has a lot of support for it, because it doesn't privilege the Mage cosmology over any other one. For example, if Fae Arcadia and Mage Arcadia are both places, then you have &quot;the real shiny true Arcadia and the shitty fake pathetic reflection of Arcadia for losers&quot;, whereas &quot;Mage Arcadia is a symbolic representation of the ideals of time and fate that a Mage creates within themself to connect their soul to the Supernal, which resembles Mage Arcadia to a point because it both draw from similar pools of symbols&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are making the mistake of assuming there is any connection between Faerie Arcadia and Supernal Arcadia at all beyond the name. They are no more connected than the Obrimos Supernal realm is connected to Demon the Descent's power stat. They are no more connected than Paris, France and Paris, Texas. It's not &quot;Real Arcadia&quot; and &quot;Fake Arcadia&quot;, it's one place that actually exists in the phenomenal world that we exist in, and one completely unrelated &quot;place&quot; that may or may not &quot;exist&quot; for a definition of the word that precludes manifesting in any phenomenal sense, and is the origin of the symbols that mages can see with their Wizard Eyes, which describe the phenomena of Fate and Time and are meaningless outside the context of those actual phenomena.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990210#post990210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see the cave allegory being something some mages tell themselves, but out of universe I don't really think it works out, unless the Supernal is the only kind of magic in the your setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plato's Allegory of the Cave is just that - an allegory. An imperfect analogy that helps describe complex and largely abstract concepts in more relatable, concrete terms. And I fail to see how the existence of a &quot;place&quot; (which, remember, has only the barest resemblance to the way we understand the word, since it has no phenomenal presence) from which symbols that describe phenomena emanate, and certain people having the ability to do magic by manipulating those symbols in any way precludes the possibility of other people doing magic by purely phenomenal means. All that said, there <i>is</i> a very pro-mage bias inherent in the allegory. Just as there was a pro-intellectual bias inherent in it when Plato originally coined it. That doesn't mean it's entirely wrong, it's just a biased way of explaining the nature of the phenomenal as one side of the coin that is reality, with the other side being the symbolic/supernal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990210#post990210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I'm just a crossover person, but I have heard a lot about how Awakening is crossover-compatible, and how quite a few Mysteries aren't connected to the Supernal and relate to other supernatural phenomena.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is accurate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990210#post990210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've also heard that mages don't approach them from the perspective of &quot;oh look at these silly little fake versions of the Supernal realms&quot;, and going deep into the symbols approach seems like a good way to do it, allowing mages to study and comprehend other supernatural phenomena and connect it to their own understanding of the world, without making either cosmology subservient to the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Err... Mages <i>do </i>attempt to explain mysteries that are not supernal in origin in a way that fits within their model. That doesn't mean other models are subservient to theirs. It just means they have a biased way of describing what they observe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-20-2016, 12:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T21:33:35-07:00","id":990256,"title":"","content":"I mean, I'm not arguing that, but Dave really went off with vehemence over the idea that mages try to force phenomena they investigate to fit their preconceptions, and I was suggesting that a major contributor to that idea (and the general idea of Mage supremacy) is the language used by the books and mages themselves. <br /> <br /> And I want there to be a connection between the two Arcadias, because, as I've said, having the Supernal be completely unconnected to all the other forms of magic is awkward and silly, at least to me. I'm trying to find a way that connects them without privileging one over the other.<br /> <br /> And again, I wouldn't mind mages being arrogant dicks if the book actually ran with this, and made it clear that Mage is a game about struggling with your own ego in a society of half-mad potential supervillains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-20-2016, 12:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T21:40:25-07:00","id":990257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990246#post990246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay then. That's...pretty much what I was saying I would like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Yes it is. As I've tried to tell you before, what you want out of Mage is not very far removed from what Mage already is. Your issues seem to stem more from refusing to meet Mage on its own terms than anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990246#post990246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think one of my major problems is in terminology: referring to everything that isn't Supernal as &quot;fallen&quot; or &quot;the lie&quot; and everyone who isn't a Mage as &quot;unawakened&quot; probably contributes more to people seeing Mage supremacy than anything in the actual content, honestly.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Fallen world (also known as the Phenomenal world) and The Lie are different, specific things. They do not refer to everything that isn't Supernal. The Fallen world is Fallen because it has been cut off from the Supernal by the Abyss, and the Lie refers specifically to the parts of reality that keep people from being able to understand the nature of the cosmos as Mages see it. And, yes, the terminology is very pro-mage biased. Because it was invented by Mages, for Mages. Don't mistake in-character bias for Mages actually being &quot;supreme&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990246#post990246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be nice if the books could be a bit more overt that those terms are mostly used by mages out of egotism. Dave went on a tear in one thread about how much he hates people assuming that mages look at all other supernatural phenomena as subordinate to the Supernal and beneath it, but it's kind of inevitable that people are going to assume that when that's the language that mages and the books use.</div> </div> </div> </div>It helps when people actually read the whole book. Not saying you necessarily didn't, but a lot (and I do mean a LOT) of this particular misconception about Mage comes more from people <i>not</i> reading what's written in Mage and only reading things that other people have written <i>about</i> Mage than from Mage actually being written in a way that fosters it. Maybe the 1e core book presented it in a misleading way, but there have been a lot of Mage books since then and the 2e core book is a hell of a lot clearer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T21:43:34-07:00","id":990258,"title":"","content":"The Supernal is connected to the other forms of magic. It gives rise and meaning to concepts like death, sight, depth, location, transition, heat, truth, and the future, all of which are necessary building blocks not just for supernatural workings, but for phenomenal existence.<br /> <br /> It's not some neat fivefold overlay that sits on top of Faerie, the Shadow, the Underworld, the Inferno, and ????. But the other gamelines don't have anything resembling that kind of wide-spanning interlocking impact on the cosmology either. Faerie isn't a great God-Machine facility gone haywire, but that's neither a problem for Changeling nor Demon. Neither is devalued; they stand on their own merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T21:50:19-07:00","id":990261,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to meet Mage on its own terms, and I would be genuinely up for advice on how to do that. <br /> <br /> I actually went back over another thread I made asking people to convince me that Mage supremacy isn't a thing, and even though I've changed my stance on Mage quite a bit since then I'm seeing a lot of bad arguments there. For example the problem with &quot;oh, that's all just Mage bias and it's actually bullshit!&quot; is that the book never says that or implies that it's particularly likely. It would be like if Mummy didn't have the ST section and just expected players to work out the truth on their own. <br /> <br /> As an example, calling the world &quot;the fallen world&quot; because it's cut off from the Supernal explicitly positions the Supernal as being &quot;better&quot; than all the other forms of magic that exist purely within the &quot;fallen&quot; world. Something like &quot;the Diamond refers to the world as &quot;the fallen world&quot; because they're trying to bring back a lost golden age, but that golden age might never have happened and bringing it back might be a very bad idea&quot; should have been emphasized way more heavily if they wanted to push the &quot;it's just in-universe Mage bias&quot; explanation more seriously. <br /> <br /> Also, question: does the Lie apply to the collective effects that keep people from seeing the supernatural? Like, shouldn't it include Lunacy and the Mask?<br /> <br /> And here are some examples of Bad Ways to Argue Against Mage Supremacy that I've noticed. Comparing the Supernal to subatomic particles implies that all other magical phenomena is made up of the Supernal, which I've repeatedly been told isn't true. &quot;The Supernal gives rise and meaning to concepts necessary for supernatural workings&quot; also ends up sounding Mage supremacist, because it makes it sound like all other magic relies on the Supernal to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-20-2016, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T21:57:31-07:00","id":990265,"title":"","content":"To put it another way: mages have insight into a particular way in which the world is built, and knowledge of that structure that allows them to rearrange it in certain ways, which we call spells and sorcery. This is the same for changelings, demons, and mummies. Changelings know how to broker deals with the voices of living phenomena; demons perceive occult complexities in ways they can exploit for reality-bending effects; mummies have an intimate understanding of the partitioned makeup of the human soul and how to draw on it for strength. Mages don't harness their own Pillars, or pledge Goblin Oaths, or use Embedded reality tricks with reflexive ease.<br /> <br /> Because of the way their particular perspective privileges understanding and picking things apart, mages may be the best equipped out of the various templates to go afield and start trying to pick apart indirect ways of studying what separates the Ab from the Ba, or how to communicate with whatever it is that signs the Contract of Hours, or what it takes for a human being to exploit Unchained physics. But they don't just have a spell that gets them from zero to understanding. They just have good research tools. Other templates can do research, too.<br /> <br /> All of it is part of a deep and complicated whole. All of it is relevant, somehow. Blind men crowd around an elephant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T21:59:19-07:00","id":990266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990261#post990261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an example, calling the world &quot;the fallen world&quot; because it's cut off from the Supernal explicitly positions the Supernal as being &quot;better&quot; than all the other forms of magic that exist purely within the &quot;fallen&quot; world.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it really doesn't. We've been talking about what the Supernal is and how it relates to reality throughout this thread, so I would like you to reread that, then examine the quoted assumption and reconsider why you come to that conclusion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, question: does the Lie apply to the collective effects that keep people from seeing the supernatural? Like, shouldn't it include Lunacy and the Mask? </div> </div> </div>It kinda sorta does. In the CofD, supernatural phenomena is common enough that it's somewhat of an open secret, but for some reason human beings often repress the memories or refuse to talk about it, which is why one of the mortal starting questions is &quot;What have you forgotten?&quot; -If- you use Awakened metaphysics - and you don't have to, outside of Mage - the Quiescent Curse is a good reason why humanity is wired to do that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 10-20-2016, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T22:02:14-07:00","id":990267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990261#post990261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually went back over another thread I made asking people to convince me that Mage supremacy isn't a thing, and even though I've changed my stance on Mage quite a bit since then I'm seeing a lot of bad arguments there. For example the problem with &quot;oh, that's all just Mage bias and it's actually bullshit!&quot; is that the book never says that or implies that it's particularly likely. It would be like if Mummy didn't have the ST section and just expected players to work out the truth on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you read the same Mage: the Awakening I did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990261#post990261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an example, calling the world &quot;the fallen world&quot; because it's cut off from the Supernal explicitly positions the Supernal as being &quot;better&quot; than all the other forms of magic that exist purely within the &quot;fallen&quot; world.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990261#post990261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something like &quot;the Diamond refers to the world as &quot;the fallen world&quot; because they're trying to bring back a lost golden age, but that golden age might never have happened and bringing it back might be a very bad idea&quot; should have been emphasized way more heavily if they wanted to push the &quot;it's just in-universe Mage bias&quot; explanation more seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Err... It sounds like you're conflating the term &quot;Fallen&quot; with a reference to the Fall of Atlantis? That's... Not why they call it that. It's fallen because it's cut off from the Supernal by the Abyss.<br /> <br /> The Supernal is not a &quot;better&quot; or &quot;more real&quot; or &quot;higher&quot; reality than the Phenomenal. Both are equal aspects of the cosmos. It's not &quot;fake reality&quot; and &quot;real reality&quot;, it's &quot;what is true&quot; and &quot;what is real&quot;. Both worlds need each other - the phenomenal needs the symbolic to define it, and the symbolic needs the phenomenal to embody it. Each is meaningless without the other, they are two sides of the same coin, and the phenomenal is &quot;Fallen&quot; because it is separated from its other side.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990261#post990261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, question: does the Lie apply to the collective effects that keep people from seeing the supernatural? Like, shouldn't it include Lunacy and the Mask?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's up to the ST, really. In my games, yes and no. Lunacy, the Mask, Quiessence, and other, similar phenomena are all different expressions of a related phenomena, which The Handbook for the Recently Deceased sums up as &quot;live people ignore the strange and unusual.&quot; Mages do ascribe this phenomenon to the Lie. Whether or not they are right, I leave open because it doesn't really make a big difference in play one way or the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T22:03:18-07:00","id":990268,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying that it's right, I'm saying that referring to something as &quot;fallen&quot; because it's separated from the Supernal even though it has plenty of other forms of magic that operate unimpeded inside it implies that the Supernal is &quot;better&quot; than those forms of magic in some way. And I'm not saying it's &quot;better&quot; or &quot;higher&quot; just that the way the books talk about it makes it completely understandable to draw that conclusion. <br /> <br /> And I do kind of prefer &quot;fallen&quot; as being almost entirely grandiose Diamond bluster that comes from their golden age obsession. <br /> <br /> One of the ways I was working on the &quot;why doesn't other magic cause paradox&quot; question in MtT was that other magic is &quot;structured&quot; in a way that what mages do isn't, and I think that's applicable to Awakening. Other supernatural beings and sorcerers exploit existing connections and phenomena, while mages basically reach into reality's guts and start moving things around, which is inherently more dangerous and less stable than, say, a Contract or an Embed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T22:06:22-07:00","id":990270,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that a lot of the terminology on Higher or Lower doesn't come from things like &quot;better or worse&quot;, but instead more the more occult meanings tied up to a thing's conceptual nature versus it's actual implementation, etc. - such as &quot;As Above, So Below&quot; or a the platonic ideal of something being defined as being the most like itself as it can be instead of being some measure of objectively better or worse.<br /> <br /> So the Fallen World isn't a worse place because it's further from the Supernal, necessarily, it's worse because what separates it from the Supernal is concentrated anti-reality which sometimes seeps in through the cracks. You could theoretically have a setting where the Fallen World is fallen simply because it's harder to do magic because of the separation between the Supernal and the Fallen world, and that would be the only consequence. Sadly, they aren't separated by a neutral vacuum but instead something that's legitimately horrible, but hey, horror story.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the Lie, the falseness that makes people unable to see the world for what it is? That's because of the Exarchs, which are a -Supernal- force.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 10-20-2016, 01:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T22:09:12-07:00","id":990272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990268#post990268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying that it's right, I'm saying that referring to something as &quot;fallen&quot; because it's separated from the Supernal even though it has plenty of other forms of magic that operate unimpeded inside it implies that the Supernal is &quot;better&quot; than those forms of magic in some way.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what way does it do that? Because I don't see that at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990268#post990268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the ways I was working on the &quot;why doesn't other magic cause paradox&quot; question in MtT was that other magic is &quot;structured&quot; in a way that what mages do isn't, and I think that's applicable to Awakening. Other supernatural beings and sorcerers exploit existing connections and phenomena, while mages basically reach into reality's guts and start moving things around, which is inherently more dangerous and less stable than, say, a Contract or an Embed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that is how it works. Non-supernal magic is phenomenal in nature - that is to say, it works on phenomena, albeit esoteric phenomena. They exploit obscure and secret rules of the real world. Supernal Magic works by altering the symbol-truths that define the phenomenal. To put it another way, non-supernal magic exploits loopholes in the laws of physics to achieve a desired result, whereas Supernal magic temporarily changes the laws of physics to make the desired result the natural one. This has the side-effect of potentially allowing unreality into the phenomenal world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T22:17:38-07:00","id":990274,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's basically what MtT ended up as. I'm thinking this is ultimately more a matter of time and emphasis. <br /> <br /> So if the Supernal isn't &quot;above&quot; other forms of magic, does that mean that other supernatural beings can become as powerful as archmages? Are the True Fae and the Machine as powerful or more powerful than the Exarchs?<br /> <br /> In general, I don't like putting up big &quot;No Other Splats Allowed&quot; signs- I think every splat should be able to roam the Astral with impunity, and Changelings and Beasts should probably be even better at it than Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T22:28:02-07:00","id":990276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990274#post990274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's basically what MtT ended up as. I'm thinking this is ultimately more a matter of time and emphasis.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's literally exactly how it works as written.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990274#post990274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if the Supernal isn't &quot;above&quot; other forms of magic, does that mean that other supernatural beings can become as powerful as archmages? Are the True Fae and the Machine as powerful or more powerful than the Exarchs?</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, other supernatural beings are... well... beings. Exarchs and Ascended Mages are just sentient supernal symbols. It's the difference between being an extant entity with power over reality and being an abstract concept that defines reality. Kind of hard to compare their &quot;power&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990274#post990274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, I don't like putting up big &quot;No Other Splats Allowed&quot; signs- I think every splat should be able to roam the Astral with impunity, and Changelings and Beasts should probably be even better at it than Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changelings interact with dreams in a way Mages can't, and have a very difficult time trying to explain within their model of the cosmos. Beasts occupy a space within the Astral that Mages have a difficult time pinning down &quot;where&quot; it is within their model. That said, the Onerios and the Temenos are pretty hard for things that aren't Mages or humans to access, because they are essentially the inside of the human soul. Hard to get to if you don't <i>have</i> a human soul. It's not a Mage thing, it's a human thing, Mages just happen to be near enough to human, soul-wise, to get there too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T22:32:08-07:00","id":990277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990274#post990274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's basically what MtT ended up as. I'm thinking this is ultimately more a matter of time and emphasis.<br /> <br /> So if the Supernal isn't &quot;above&quot; other forms of magic, does that mean that other supernatural beings can become as powerful as archmages? Are the True Fae and the Machine as powerful or more powerful than the Exarchs?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are spirits and archangels that exist on that level, and while there's no power tier breakdown between super duper cosmological beings, you can definitely see the God-Machine, the Principle, etc. as supernatural phenomena on the same level as the Exarchs, sure.<br /> <br /> Archmages are fairly unique among theoretically playable characters in their power scale because that type of power is often at best completely removed and at worst actively harmful to the feeling of horror that these games go for; for Mage, it works precisely BECAUSE it's a game about the horrors of hubris, abuse of power, etc. etc., and <i>even then</i> archmages are most often used as plot hooks or NPCs; playable archmages are a niche, niche, <i>niche</i> game that is as wildly different from being a regular mage as being a mage is different from being a human. It's not a natural continuation, it's a weirdass offshoot into obssession and power that comes with unimaginable baggage. Other splats might eventually get stuff that plays in upper power playspace - I'm looking forward to the vampire Elder book that's being written - but I would caution against looking at the lack of playable peers among archmages as a lack of parity to be rectified, because it's not.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T22:34:13-07:00","id":990278,"title":"","content":"That gets into a whole other issue- having the most powerful splat be the one that has the least downsides and is the most human. The only way to give characters great power while maintaining an atmosphere of horror is to make that power inherently monstrous and dehumanizing. Power or humanity, choose one. It's why Prometheans don't get to keep their Transmutations if they ND into a human. Requiem 2e actually makes it so that using your powers dings your humanity, right? <br /> <br /> I'd probably just rule that anyone can access the Astral, it's just that Mages have the easiest time getting their initially- they aren't any more human than the other splats.<br /> <br /> And about archmages, I had less of a problem with them when I realized that they're pretty much comparable to changelings becoming True Fae- a usually undesired outcome that makes the character utterly inhuman and unplayable without special rules. Though archmages, at least according to imperial mysteries, are still more powerful than True Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T22:48:34-07:00","id":990281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990278#post990278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That gets into a whole other issue- having the most powerful splat be the one that has the least downsides and is the most human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being the most human also means they're the most vulnerable. Mages are supper glass cannon-y. You want to kill a vampire, bring stakes and fire. You want to kill a werewolf, bring silver. You want to kill a Mage? Just shoot him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990278#post990278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only way to give characters great power while maintaining an atmosphere of horror is to make that power inherently monstrous and dehumanizing. Power or humanity, choose one. It's why Prometheans don't get to keep their Transmutations if they ND into a human. Requiem 2e actually makes it so that using your powers dings your humanity, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's almost like being human <i>is </i>a weakness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T22:54:51-07:00","id":990284,"title":"","content":"Pffffft, mages have tons of ways they can survive a bullet. Mages are super overpowered compared to others, though, and I would still prefer they had some seriously major downsides. Also? Being human is usually presented as a strength in ChroD, because it means you're able to function socially and within the human world. But that's another topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T22:58:50-07:00","id":990286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990281#post990281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being the most human also means they're the most vulnerable. Mages are supper glass cannon-y. You want to kill a vampire, bring stakes and fire. You want to kill a werewolf, bring silver. You want to kill a Mage? Just shoot him.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's almost like being human <i>is </i>a weakness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Talking in general, not to Charlaquin: I have a feeling that this is going to degenerate into another a routine debate about parity among splats, which is a non-starter even for crossover enthusiasts. I can't stop it from happening again, obviously, but I would suggest going a different direction, like maybe let's talk about why or why not being able to travel to the Astral is important at all to the splats. What does it do for them thematically? I know a locked door seems frustrating, but think of it this way: is it really an issue that a Sin-Eater can't step through the Gauntlet? In my opinion, no, because spirit stuff doesn't mesh with the Sin-Eater narrative all that well.<br /> <br /> For the same reason, the relative inaccessibility of the Astral doesn't bother me because for most splats, I don't see why playing around with the realm of ideas and the souls really helps most of them from a thematic standpoint. Remember, it's not about parity, it's about what works best for a splat's particular narrative and playstyle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 10-20-2016, 02:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T23:02:57-07:00","id":990287,"title":"","content":"Back on that, I've always thought that exploring the astral works remarkably well for Changelings. And just because SEs can't cross the gauntlet normally doesn't mean that they couldn't somehow end up in the Shadow if there's a compelling plot reason for them to be there. And wait, Demons have that power that lets them enter the astral, right? I guess it's not that big of an issue. And for the record, my issue with mages isn't so much about power as balancing power with theme. If you're throwing fireballs around with impunity and your soul doesn't at least look like something you'd find in the dumpster behind an Italian restaurant, it just doesn't feel like ChroD to me. <br /> <br /> This thread has actually been really helpful, thank you for all your posts and explanations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T23:04:48-07:00","id":990288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990286#post990286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember, it's not about parity, it's about what works best for a splat's particular narrative and playstyle.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'm spitballing, an example of what I mean is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/888441-the-pack-is-here?p=889601#post889601\">here</a>, where I argue that it's a good thing that werewolves have a restriction for crossing the Gauntlet that Mages lack, because of what it <i>means</i> to the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T01:02:37-07:00","id":990325,"title":"","content":"There's some things in this thread that are... Incorrect. Putting it charitably, and I just know Gecko's going to ignore what the books say in favour of what someone on a thread once told her, even if they didn't know what they were talking about, so, in no particular order:<br /> <br /> Beasts have a much easier time navigating the astral than mages do, strictly by mechanics. Where the Primordial Dream is is not in any way mysterious: It's the area around the Omphalos at the far end of Temenos.<br /> <br /> Only mages and beings with Integrity have an Onerios. Only those and Beasts have a personal connection to the Temenos. This is because those realms are the inside of a human soul, and nothing else has one. Other supenatural beings like demons can get powers to let them enter someone *else's* soul, or have a beast pull them into the temenos with its powers.<br /> <br /> The world isn't Fallen because it's not the Supernal - there was a world before the Fall - but because it's damaged by the Abyss.<br /> <br /> The Supernal Realm is not a physical place, and destroys anything that tries to treat it like one.<br /> <br /> Other supernatural beings have Supernal symbols over them when viewed in Mage Sight, but then so does *everything*. Mages don't believe vampires are linked to Stygia just because they show up in Death Sight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T01:18:49-07:00","id":990329,"title":"","content":"I'm not going to ignore that, and it all sounds pretty good. I'm genuinely trying to get a handle on this, so can we chill? And I pretty much said, several times, that I was speaking in terms of what people assume and not what the books actually say. I even explicitly spelled out several times that I was talking about what gave rise to misconceptions people had. So can we maybe just...chill? If you want, you could make a list of things you don't want me to do, so I'd know specifically.<br /> <br /> That said, while we have you here, your posts about how you see a connection between the Hedge and the Astral are fascinating and I would love to hear more about that, especially as it relates to Changelings. Oh, and what is the Arcadia/Astral connection? I could see the Gentry wanting to get their hands on human souls so they could break in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-20-2016, 04:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T01:23:00-07:00","id":990331,"title":"","content":"Emanations aren't actually in the Supernal - they're pockets of material reality heavily influenced by it. If a demense is, say, 90% Fallen and 10% Supernal, an Emanation is closer to 50:50. As Mage *says*, every Emanation has a rip to the Supernal in it. Which kills anyone using it, because the Supernal does that unless you're Ascended or have the ability and know-how to create a Lustrum and interpret it into an experience its safe to comprehend. This is exactly and deliberately like the gates to the Supernal found at the end of archmages' Godlen Roads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T01:44:12-07:00","id":990341,"title":"","content":"That wasn't aimed at you, Gecko, rather the people who appeared to be feeding you their headcanon, which you've had trouble parsing from the books before.<br /> <br /> So, changelings don't have anything to do with the astral. As of 1st ed, they even physically bounced off portals to Temenos. I don't think going that far is necessary, but the relationship between dreams and the hedge is like programs running in a holodeck: Changelings can view dreams from the hedge, and step into them such that they're in physical form unlike everyone else. <br /> <br /> Well, the viewing part works from the Onieros, too: You can squat in someone's soul and watch their thoughts and dreams, assuming their soul's inner ecology of Goetia don't turn on you like in Inception.<br /> <br /> This does not mean that the Hedge and Oneiros are connected. Just that they both view dreams. The Hedge and Faerie could be off on a right-angle to the Astral.<br /> <br /> So, a few options suggest themselves:<br /> <br /> The Hedge thorns hurt souls, and the Gebtry are voracious consumers of story. Perhaps it is a Lower Depth, and Faerie is part of it.<br /> <br /> The contract-based nature if changeling reality and the appearance of the Hedge might suggest some connection to Supernal Arcadia even if they're not the same (Mage-Arcadia's &quot;thorns&quot; look like silver cracks in reality, the name being an apt description that confuses first-time crossover readers). Perhaps, then, Faerie-and-the-Hedge is a particularly large and active Emanation Realm.<br /> <br /> When mages enter the Astral, they pass through a symbolic barrier between dreams and the Onerios that hurt like hell to move through. In the same way that Mages and Werewolves are aware that the Gauntlet has stuff (even native life forms) in it but their powers treat it as a barrier to be crossed, perhaps the Astral Barrier is actually the Hedge? It is dream-adjacent, a realm of narrative would seem logically placed between dreams and the personal soul, and the pain mages experience when crossing seems analogous to the thorns.<br /> <br /> The third one came to me long after changeling 2e was written, and I'm reasonably proud if it. I have no intention of making any one of them canon. Some things *are* best left multiple-choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T01:55:15-07:00","id":990347,"title":"","content":"That's all cool as hell, thank you! By the way, will you be working on the Crossover Chronicle? Just seeing the bits of crossover theories you've posted for Mage, I feel like you'd come up with some great stuff for it.<br /> <br /> Also, would it be accurate to say that the difference between the Supernal and the Lower Depths is that the Supernal has All Of The Things while the Lower Depths have No Things? So, for example, there could be a lower depth where the concept of time doesn't exist. In the Supernal, however, the concept of time exists, but it hyper-exists. The Supernal has All Of The Time. All of it. At once. <br /> <br /> To use another analogy, the Supernal seems to be sort of like the sun, in that it's a power source that will burn your goddamn face off and give you cancer if you get too close to it or get careless with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-20-2016, 05:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T02:42:35-07:00","id":990355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990347#post990347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, would it be accurate to say that the difference between the Supernal and the Lower Depths is that the Supernal has All Of The Things while the Lower Depths have No Things?</div> </div> </div> </div>For clarity I think it would be better to say that the Lower Depths have Some Things, and the Abyss has No Things (though it has some things that aren't things, possibly all things that aren't things).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T02:49:14-07:00","id":990356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990325#post990325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The world isn't Fallen because it's not the Supernal - there was a world before the Fall - but because it's damaged by the Abyss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, okay. That one's partially on me, then. I knew that there was a world before the Fall, but that it was the relative separation after the fact that made it &quot;Fallen&quot;, although the interpretation I was working under was academic anyways, so. Thanks for clearing up the misunderstanding.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T03:43:28-07:00","id":990361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990355#post990355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For clarity I think it would be better to say that the Lower Depths have Some Things, and the Abyss has No Things (though it has some things that aren't things, possibly all things that aren't things).</div> </div> </div> </div>Or to be more precise, that which is from the Lower Depths is inimical because it lacks sufficient thingness, and acts like a vaccuum, drawing whatever thingness the particular manifestation lacks out of the world around it. This can be a problem when that thingness is something like &quot;location&quot; or &quot;identity.&quot;<br /> <br /> That which is of the Abyss is inimical because it has incompatible thingness. Abyssal manifestations exhibit properties that contradict sense and causality. This can be a problem when it means multiple timelines and histories begin to coexist and overlap one another, or when competing laws of physics take on the contagious properties of disease.<br /> <br /> Direct submergence in the Supernal Realm, without the protection of a lustrum, is inimical because it has excessive or overwhelming thingness. This can be a problem like when your computer overclocks and runs operations it's seriously not equipped for, overheats and crashes, and your hardware is damaged and your data destroyed. In this analogy, the data is you as a person, your entire existence, backward and forward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T03:49:53-07:00","id":990362,"title":"","content":"So the Fallen world is really fallen from the world it used to be, when the Abyss wasn't in the way people using Supernal magic manipulate reality. Fallen in the sense of not being in that idealized golden age.<br /> <br /> As for the Hedge and Arcadia, I like that its one of the most confusing and dangerous places in the Cosmology for Mages, it just doesn't fit perfectly in ANY catogory and as such probably drives Mages nuts with frustration and curiousity.<br /> <br /> I also find it interesting that only Mage and characters with interigity stat produce Onieros in they're souls.<br /> <br /> Why that is would be a curious discussion, plus the Onieros of the something like a Fae Touched or a Ghoul who has been around for a millenia would be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 10-20-2016, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T04:33:58-07:00","id":990366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990361#post990361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or to be more precise, that which is from the Lower Depths is inimical because it lacks sufficient thingness, and acts like a vaccuum, drawing whatever thingness the particular manifestation lacks out of the world around it. This can be a problem when that thingness is something like &amp;quot;location&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;identity.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> That which is of the Abyss is inimical because it has incompatible thingness. Abyssal manifestations exhibit properties that contradict sense and causality. This can be a problem when it means multiple timelines and histories begin to coexist and overlap one another, or when competing laws of physics take on the contagious properties of disease.<br /> <br /> Direct submergence in the Supernal Realm, without the protection of a lustrum, is inimical because it has excessive or overwhelming thingness. This can be a problem like when your computer overclocks and runs operations it's seriously not equipped for, overheats and crashes, and your hardware is damaged and your data destroyed. In this analogy, the data is you as a person, your entire existence, backward and forward.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is a good description of the three non-Fallen worlds.<br /> <br /> The Shadow, Underworld, Astral, and Material realms are are part of the Fallen World: They have sufficient thingness to exist, but not so much that they overheat, and some incompatible elements have crept in like bugs in code.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T13:27:05-07:00","id":990593,"title":"","content":"This discussion has made me like 2e even more, because it really does resolve a lot of misconceptions and complaints. It does so in a fairly complicated way that I didn't initially &quot;get&quot;, but that's not really a criticism. I'm fine with the game about wizards and cosmic secrets being deliberately complicated and somewhat obtuse. It really makes the players feel like they're solving mysteries. <br /> <br /> I guess another thing I don't like about the &quot;source code&quot; example, and why I prefer the &quot;sun&quot; or &quot;turning lies into truth&quot; analogies, is because reality hacking is kind of already Demon's hat. Part of what threw me on that was misinterpreting the whole Supernal vs. Fallen terminology as &quot;the Supernal is the true world and everything else is fake garbage&quot;, which I see now isn't how it works. <br /> <br /> To put it another way, my initial conception of the how Awakening worked was &quot;there are five Magic Space Heavens with magic pieces of paper in them and if you write your name on one you turn into a Mage&quot;, which is also not how it works at all. <br /> <br /> The Awakening and the whole &quot;name writing&quot; thing are metaphors/analogies, but they're metaphors and analogies that mages make real, because that's what magic does. The Supernal realms could be seen as the Mage imposing order on the raw power of the Supernal and turning it into a form they can comprehend, which allows them to form a connection between it and their soul. To use another example, when a Supernal summoner summons a Fate entity that resembles an elven sage (that happens to resemble a Fae), he's not actually opening a portal to the Elf World and summoning someone from there. What he's doing is imposing the analogy of &quot;elf sage&quot; on the raw concept of fate. Or, to put it another way, &quot;raw fate&quot; can't just exist as raw fate or be understood in our reality, but it can be understood as being symbolically and conceptually similar to an elven sage, so it manifests in the shape of one. It's similarity to the Fae isn't because it is one of them as much as because it possesses the same symbols that that define them. A Mage could summon an entity from a Phenomenal realm, but would do so by using the Symbols connected to it. Sorry if all of this is obvious, I'm getting a handle on it and it's pretty cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T13:55:28-07:00","id":990612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990593#post990593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> because reality hacking is kind of already Demon's hat. </div> </div> </div> </div>Note that Mage: The Awakening predates Demon: The Descent by about a decade, and if you consider the &quot;reality hacking&quot; themes and powers of M:TAw 's progenitor, Mage: The Ascension, add yet another decade.<br /> <br /> If anything, Demon is appropriating Mage's splat abilities and setting elements, not the other way around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T14:03:46-07:00","id":990620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990593#post990593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This discussion has made me like 2e even more, because it really does resolve a lot of misconceptions and complaints. It does so in a fairly complicated way that I didn't initially &quot;get&quot;, but that's not really a criticism. I'm fine with the game about wizards and cosmic secrets being deliberately complicated and somewhat obtuse. It really makes the players feel like they're solving mysteries.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel you. I really didn't get Awakening either until the2e dev blogs. Though, I didn't exactly try very hard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990593#post990593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess another thing I don't like about the &quot;source code&quot; example, and why I prefer the &quot;sun&quot; or &quot;turning lies into truth&quot; analogies, is because reality hacking is kind of already Demon's hat. Part of what threw me on that was misinterpreting the whole Supernal vs. Fallen terminology as &quot;the Supernal is the true world and everything else is fake garbage&quot;, which I see now isn't how it works. <br /> <br /> To put it another way, my initial conception of the how Awakening worked was &quot;there are five Magic Space Heavens with magic pieces of paper in them and if you write your name on one you turn into a Mage&quot;, which is also not how it works at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the 1e core book did very much give the magic space heaven impression of the Supernal.<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;source code of the Matrix&quot; analogy, yeah, reality hacking is more Demon's wheelhouse than Mages. It's just a convenient metaphor because The Matrix was a lot of folks first brush with Gnostic philosophy, which Mage (and Demon) is highly informed by.<br /> <br /> Actually I think the best way to map The Matrix to Awakening would not be to say that the Matrix is the phenomenal and the real world is the Supernal, but to say that the Matrix is <i>The Astral</i>, the code is the Supernal, and the &quot;real&quot; world is the phenomenal. That's why Neo's powers work in the real world in the sequels, the first movie was the story of his Awakening, blowing up Agent Smith at the end was signing his name on the Watchtower, and in the sequels he understood that the real world was just as bound by the symbolic laws as the Matrix and was just as mutable.<br /> <br /> [edit]Oh, and the Mobil Avenue train station was a Lower Depth. Possibly the Hell of an Unchained Trainman? Not sure, that scene was weird.[/edit]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990593#post990593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Awakening and the whole &quot;name writing&quot; thing are metaphors/analogies, but they're metaphors and analogies that mages make real, because that's what magic does. The Supernal realms could be seen as the Mage imposing order on the raw power of the Supernal and turning it into a form they can comprehend, which allows them to form a connection between it and their soul. To use another example, when a Supernal summoner summons a Fate entity that resembles an elven sage (that happens to resemble a Fae), he's not actually opening a portal to the Elf World and summoning someone from there. What he's doing is imposing the analogy of &quot;elf sage&quot; on the raw concept of fate. Or, to put it another way, &quot;raw fate&quot; can't just exist as raw fate or be understood in our reality, but it can be understood as being symbolically and conceptually similar to an elven sage, so it manifests in the shape of one. It's similarity to the Fae isn't because it is one of them as much as because it possesses the same symbols that that define them. A Mage could summon an entity from a Phenomenal realm, but would do so by using the Symbols connected to it. Sorry if all of this is obvious, I'm getting a handle on it and it's pretty cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've got it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-20-2016, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T14:11:57-07:00","id":990626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990325#post990325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts have a much easier time navigating the astral than mages do, strictly by mechanics. Where the Primordial Dream is is not in any way mysterious: It's the area around the Omphalos at the far end of Temenos.</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad there. My Beast knowledge is severely limited, and my Astral knowledge is still developing. Thank you for clarifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T14:31:40-07:00","id":990634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990612#post990612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Note that Mage: The Awakening predates Demon: The Descent by about a decade, and if you consider the &amp;quot;reality hacking&amp;quot; themes and powers of M:TAw 's progenitor, Mage: The Ascension, add yet another decade.<br /> <br /> If anything, Demon is appropriating Mage's splat abilities and setting elements, not the other way around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage 2e came out after Demon and the GMC. Mage by its nature is one of the wider ChroD games thematically, so hacking isn't its only hat. I'm saying that in a post-GMC world where Demon exists, which 2e took into account, I like reality hacking being Demon's hat and Supernal magic using different metaphors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T14:43:07-07:00","id":990640,"title":"","content":"My personal headcanon is that the Changeling Arcadia is a shadow of the Supernal Arcadia.<br /> <br /> <br /> Colleen","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T14:54:34-07:00","id":990649,"title":"","content":"Well, if you compare the Supernal to the sun, which I like, you could say that everything is its shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T14:57:56-07:00","id":990651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990649#post990649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if you compare the Supernal to the sun, which I like, you could say that everything is its shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>The interplay between light, objects, and shadows is actually much closer to the source metaphor than computers and programming, so I'd say this is a pretty apropos way of looking at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-20-2016, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T15:18:30-07:00","id":990661,"title":"","content":"Plus, the sun analogy, unlike the data analogy, captures how dangerous the Supernal is, and how whether it's a physical location or not doesn't really matter, because trying to go to it or enter it is roughly equivalent to trying to land on the sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T16:49:21-07:00","id":990685,"title":"","content":"Hello.<br /> <br /> If I may go back a little (sorry, I was gone for a while because of work), I would like to rekindle the discussion about mages manipulating the building blocs of reality and that making them stronger than anyone else, according to some people.<br /> <br /> My understanding of the problem is more akin to the difference between physics and ingeniering. Theoretical physicists may manipulate something more fundamental but it takes time, efforts and money to turn their work into something useful. Ingenier may work with some grosser aspect of reality but it is easier to turn it into something which can have an &quot;effect&quot; in day to day lives, they'll just attain a lesser level of understanding of the finest points of how it works. In the end, they manipulate the same laws but not in the same way and if each one can manage to produce the results of the other it will take an insane amount of time and efforts for it to work out. Mages explaining that because they manipulate it unfiltered and at a more fundamental level, they are better and more powerful than, say, the werewolves is like Sheldon Cooper telling Howard Wollowitz that, even though he's MIT-trained and has been an astronaut, he's inferior to him. And that is fitting to a game of hubris.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","name":"Lokiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T17:12:51-07:00","id":990695,"title":"","content":"No, please! Don't bring the Bing Bong Brothers into this! I yield! I'll do anything you want! No more!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T22:07:11-07:00","id":990794,"title":"","content":"Hm, I'd be interested in working out how various features map to the sun analogy, because I could see it being a popular one. <br /> <br /> Also, about the Lie- what if the mechanisms vampires have to hide evidence of their feeding are an abstract manifestation of it? This also shows the difference between mages and other supernatural beings- vampires have a convenient, prepackaged way to hide evidence of themselves that doesn't risk poking holes in reality, unlike with mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T22:28:42-07:00","id":990801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990794#post990794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, about the Lie- what if the mechanisms vampires have to hide evidence of their feeding are an abstract manifestation of it? This also shows the difference between mages and other supernatural beings- vampires have a convenient, prepackaged way to hide evidence of themselves that doesn't risk poking holes in reality, unlike with mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>The beauty of the &quot;shadows cast by the light of truth&quot; interpretation is that things like werewolves' Lunacy and mortals' general Integrity breaking points being independent phenomena with their own causes and rationales is not mutually exclusive with them also being shadows cast by the Lie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T18:23:29-07:00","id":991203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990620#post990620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually I think the best way to map The Matrix to Awakening would not be to say that the Matrix is the phenomenal and the real world is the Supernal, but to say that the Matrix is <i>The Astral</i>, the code is the Supernal, and the &quot;real&quot; world is the phenomenal. That's why Neo's powers work in the real world in the sequels, the first movie was the story of his Awakening, blowing up Agent Smith at the end was signing his name on the Watchtower, and in the sequels he understood that the real world was just as bound by the symbolic laws as the Matrix and was just as mutable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wish I'd made the connection between the Matrix and the Astral sooner.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990620#post990620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[edit]Oh, and the Mobil Avenue train station was a Lower Depth. Possibly the Hell of an Unchained Trainman? Not sure, that scene was weird.[/edit]</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. Limbo is the Trainman's Cintamani. The train is the Iris. He's not an archmaster, though; the analogy has to break down <i>somewhere</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T19:16:28-07:00","id":991218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990801#post990801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The beauty of the &amp;quot;shadows cast by the light of truth&amp;quot; interpretation is that things like werewolves' Lunacy and mortals' general Integrity breaking points being independent phenomena with their own causes and rationales is not mutually exclusive with them also being shadows cast by the Lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>In general, what I love about the &quot;symbols&quot; focus is that it allows supernatural phenomena to be their own things while not being completely disconnected from the Supernal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T13:00:27-07:00","id":991969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms#post990170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies since this has been discussed before, but I'm trying to get a handle on this, since I've been rereading Changeling. So, 2e has done a lot to sort of cut through the confusion on the realms, and specifying that the Arcadias aren't the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually play with this quite a lot, despite it being explicitly disavowed now.<br /> In order to heighten certain aspects of drama and storytelling, I've had Arcadian Awakenings encounter changelings and vice versa. Once I had a mage come back with a partial Mien because they made deals to survive there. There's still a demarcation between the Supernal and the Fallen here, but it's not a <i>clear</i> one, and that ambiguity is a Mystery in and of itself.<br /> <br /> So the short version is that the Supernal Realms both <i>are</i> and <i>are not</i> places. Imperial Mysteries hits on this a bit - the only way a lower-order being can perceive the Supernal is through a Lustrum, which is to say their soul struggles to perceive the symbols it's being bombarded with into a relatable format.<br /> <br /> You might say that the Supernal therefore <i>is</i> a place, but its geography isn't based on what we would consider geography, it's a relational process of symbolism, similar to but far more permanent and real than dreams. The Arcana of Space, Time, Matter, Life, and Forces all still exist in each realm, even if one is heightened over another, and there is nothing <i>less</i> real about a rock encountered in the Supernal and a rock encountered in the Fallen World (indeed, that rock is far <i>more</i> real for being what it is, a reflection of symbolic interactions.) Two people can perceive the same rock on different Lustrums, and it is still the same rock, but their perception of it will differ. Its physical and temporal relation to its environment will change, too, and so will the environment.<br /> <br /> Presumably the Ascended all have a much purer view of it.<br /> <br /> The Supernal still influences things on the Fallen World, because everything on the Fallen World is a dim reflection of the truer concepts of the Supernal Realms. Before the World was Fallen, it presumably had more of that majesty, with the Subtle Arcana more fully expressed and visible and with Supernal Beings able to jaunt on down/up.<br /> <br /> Part of the reason why this is so confusing and weird is that you are a Fallen Being, more or less. Presumably you don't have access to divine magic! You have no capacity to directly perceive the universe in the way that an Ascended Being does<br /> <br /> The reason for the primacy of Mage (and something I feel nWoD does so much better than oWoD) is that mages reflect <i>divine first causes.</i> All other forms of magic are fundamentally &quot;natural&quot;, in a sense. They're consequences of Fallen laws, even if some of those are occult laws that are beyond the sight of mortal beings (and even if those Fallen causes have Supernal antecedents - it's mentioned quite clearly that Werewolves and Vampires and other major templates all have Supernal backing at some level.) What makes a Mage special is their ability to draw down that Supernal, divine radiance to change the world, a true Alchemy in the sense of Hermes Trismegristis, who (or at least, the author claiming to be him) stated in the <i>Emerald Tablet</i> &quot;As Above, So Below.&quot; He was essentially referring to the idea that a true magician makes a change in the divine realms that is then reflected here on the physical, and, arguably, vice versa (this especially is the argument of the Free Council, who posit that the Supernal is changed in response to Fallen action as well as vice versa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T13:45:11-07:00","id":991992,"title":"","content":"I mean, it's fine if you like that explanation, but it goes right back to the problem of privileging mages and fheir related phenomena over everything else in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T04:14:19-08:00","id":1004870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990325#post990325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's some things in this thread that are... Incorrect. Putting it charitably, and I just know Gecko's going to ignore what the books say in favour of what someone on a thread once told her, even if they didn't know what they were talking about, so, in no particular order:<br /> <br /> Beasts have a much easier time navigating the astral than mages do, strictly by mechanics. Where the Primordial Dream is is not in any way mysterious: It's the area around the Omphalos at the far end of Temenos.<br /> <br /> Only mages and beings with Integrity have an Onerios. Only those and Beasts have a personal connection to the Temenos. This is because those realms are the inside of a human soul, and nothing else has one. Other supenatural beings like demons can get powers to let them enter someone *else's* soul, or have a beast pull them into the temenos with its powers.<br /> <br /> The world isn't Fallen because it's not the Supernal - there was a world before the Fall - but because it's damaged by the Abyss.<br /> <br /> The Supernal Realm is not a physical place, and destroys anything that tries to treat it like one.<br /> <br /> Other supernatural beings have Supernal symbols over them when viewed in Mage Sight, but then so does *everything*. Mages don't believe vampires are linked to Stygia just because they show up in Death Sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so the Supernal Realms aren't a physical place. Sure, I can get that a realm made up of the symbols that order reality isn't a place. But what the heck does it mean, then, for summoned beings to exist? Or for someone to ascend into the supernal realms and still be alive? Or for the Exarchs to exist as beings with will? I guess what I'm asking is how the heck can you have a living symbol? I can't really wrap my mind around that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T04:24:43-08:00","id":1004873,"title":"","content":"Have you read Imperial Mysteries? Anyway. Summoned beings are ideas that are forced upon fabric of tellurian and wear it as s body. Ascending is so difficult exactly because you have to merge/translate those symbols and force themself to part of supernal and not a guest who can be shredded by supernal winds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 11-18-2016, 07:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T05:20:38-08:00","id":1004889,"title":"","content":"I'm tempted to suggest that it IS inconceivable and that's the point. All you can do is run with it. Though that may just be me being unable to expalin it coherently.<br /> <br /> As an aside it's also worth mentioning that the Exarchs specifically are a special case. It's never outright stated (though Dave has said it explicitly) that the Exarchs physically entering the Supernal was the first paradox. That's where the Abyss starts to creep into the world.<br /> <br /> It could also be inferred that potentially all the Ascended and arch-masters are a product of the Celestial Ladder. You don't need a magic machine to ascend in the present, so why did the Atlanteans need one? There are ways around that, but it's a interesting idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T06:09:20-08:00","id":1004899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=1004873#post1004873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you read Imperial Mysteries? Anyway. Summoned beings are ideas that are forced upon fabric of tellurian and wear it as s body. Ascending is so difficult exactly because you have to merge/translate those symbols and force themself to part of supernal and not a guest who can be shredded by supernal winds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imperial Mysteries was written for an edition that considered the Supernal Realms another place as well as a collection of the symbols that order reality. 2e has gone to decent lengths to erase the former as being a part of the game. In many ways it makes more sense that way, especially if you are emphasizing that these symbols ARE the symbols that Plato talked about and not just symbols of power. However, that's a VERY different take on it than existed in 1e (which allowed for the shenanigans of Broken diamond and Soul Cages).<br /> <br /> To be fair, though, it has been a while since I've read Imperial Mysteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T06:15:04-08:00","id":1004902,"title":"","content":"Wrong, the Supernal Realms have never been a place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T06:37:51-08:00","id":1004908,"title":"","content":"They were always a realm of symbols but archmages are capable of inhabiting it by shaping them into places that resemble the fallen. And yes, being an archmages makes you a god but you still need a bubble of your will to be safe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T12:36:11-08:00","id":1005809,"title":"","content":"Not a bubble of your will, no. That's a key difference between Ascension and Awakening: Ascension is Will-based, whereas Awakening is Imago-based. That's what a Lustrum is: an Imago that allows the archmaster to make some sense of the Supernal. <br /> <br /> \u200bOn another note: if the Exarchs triggered the first Paradox, was no one able to exceed their Reach before then? Because in the context of 2e, you get Paradox if you exceed your Reach. So if there was no Paradox before the Exarchs, either no one could exceed their Reach back then or everyone could do so without fear of Paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T19:41:44-08:00","id":1005944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=1005809#post1005809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a bubble of your will, no. That's a key difference between Ascension and Awakening: Ascension is Will-based, whereas Awakening is Imago-based. That's what a Lustrum is: an Imago that allows the archmaster to make some sense of the Supernal.<br /> <br /> \u200bOn another note: if the Exarchs triggered the first Paradox, was no one able to exceed their Reach before then? Because in the context of 2e, you get Paradox if you exceed your Reach. So if there was no Paradox before the Exarchs, either no one could exceed their Reach back then or everyone could do so without fear of Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, summoned Supernal entities have unlimited Reach, don't they? Maybe it really was like that for everyone. The Silver Ladder would certainly interpret it that way, to reinforce their narrative of how the Exarchs kicked the Ladder away once they got up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T04:42:16-08:00","id":1006118,"title":"","content":"They may still have made mistakes. The difference now is that the Abyss greatly exacerbates mistakes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T11:00:07-08:00","id":1006287,"title":"","content":"The Supernal may be the source code of reality, but the source code isn't the most fundamental level of a computer. Mages may be hackers, but demons are <a href=\"http://www.catb.org/jargon/html/story-of-mel.html\" target=\"_blank\">Real Programmers.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/40-dspaul","name":"DSPaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T15:31:07-08:00","id":1006431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DSPaul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=1006287#post1006287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Supernal may be the source code of reality, but the source code isn't the most fundamental level of a computer. Mages may be hackers, but demons are <a href=\"http://www.catb.org/jargon/html/story-of-mel.html\" target=\"_blank\">Real Programmers.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Was actually expecting <a href=\"http://xkcd.com/378/\" target=\"_blank\">this link</a>, but I can't disapprove of anyone linking to the Jargon File.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T19:30:04-08:00","id":1006514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=1006431#post1006431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was actually expecting <a href=\"http://xkcd.com/378/\" target=\"_blank\">this link</a>, but I can't disapprove of anyone linking to the Jargon File.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I can't help it, <a href=\"https://xkcd.com/224/\" target=\"_blank\">Mages use Lisp, but it's obvious that Demon's use Perl</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T09:16:32-08:00","id":1006748,"title":"","content":"I will note that with the physics thing brought up earlier. The idea that &quot;things reduce to physics, so physicists are most important&quot; is something that I see bandied about often by non-scientists and physicists. There is actually a considerable amount of literary push-back against reductionism like that out there, especially in biology where the physics explanation might be handy in principle, is often useless in practice of actually understanding various aspects of selection, population change and ecology.<br /> <br /> It's all moving sunlight and geothermal heat at the end of the day, but biologists are just generally not interested in that and a lot of the tools that let you <i>do</i> physics are not going to be useful in biology. So this idea that magi understand some underlying aspect of the Truth to me is kind of moot. They have a particular language, view and framework which might just not be useful in how other supernatural beings operate and think. Even if they can be explained in a mage's context, this doesn't give mages to me &quot;authority&quot; over the way the world is, in a sense.<br /> <br /> This is coming from a pretty ardent anti-reductionist scientific pluralist, mind. So take things as you will with that.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}